ts/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_beside_another_act_in_its_registry_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_naming_the_row_and_the_mark; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_MEANING_BLESS_reattestation_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_row_tagged_two_ways_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_ruling_the_row_plain_MEANING_is_refused_naming_the_verdict; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_blessing_the_row_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_carrying_a_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_whole; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_with_a_blessed_reattestation_merges\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3559,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3559,"newLines":6,"lines":[" tier = \"Smoke\""," expected = \"The bless mark reads MEANING to every rulings reader, and only an unambiguous marked row is blessed. From an accepted verdict and its binding as committed at a revision, the act assembler derives every authorized act that the revision's committed registries and records do not carry in full. Each authorized row is owed or taken by its committed status and whole-row recorded copy; any unrecognized state or unmatched tier refuses the whole derivation naming the row. An uncommitted, unbound, non-accepted or invalid verdict, a class deriving no act, a verdict with no remaining authorized act, or an approval without an approval record refuses the whole derivation naming why. The derived acts list amendment before first approval, and their brief is filled in full or not at all. A re-attest of a row absent from the committed registries is a retirement: it is owed while its recorded copy holds the row and taken once the copy does not; on a held rung it derives no act. A first approval of an absent row is inconsistent and refuses naming the row. Each row's act follows the held-rung policy that also informs the judging brief, with the bless mark as the added condition for a released-rung MEANING row.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_MEANING_BLESS_row_reads_MEANING_and_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_an_unmarked_MEANING_row_is_not_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_row_tagged_both_ways_is_not_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_each_unaccepted_or_unreadable_verdict_is_refused_naming_why; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_mixed_first_approval_verdict_approves_only_its_approved_rows_registries; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_MEANING_row_without_the_bless_mark_is_left_unacted; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_blessed_MEANING_row_on_a_released_rung_is_reattested; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_blessed_MEANING_row_on_a_held_rung_is_left_unacted; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_rung_CLARITY_row_is_reattested_naming_its_verdict; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_rung_APPROVE_row_owes_no_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_combined_verdict_lists_the_amendment_act_before_the_first_approval_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_combined_act_interrupted_between_its_commits_lists_only_the_first_approval_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_flip_committed_without_its_copy_is_refused_naming_the_row; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_Drafted_row_present_unchanged_in_a_whole_registry_copy_is_owed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_reattest_of_a_row_below_Approved_is_refused_naming_the_row; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_completed_act_owes_none_and_is_refused; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_the_rendered_act_commands_survive_a_shell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_the_act_reads_HEAD_not_the_working_tree; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_the_composed_act_brief_names_its_verdict_and_trailer; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_two_registry_act_says_which_rows_each_approves_token_covers; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::tes